# Byte-identical checkouts on every platform.
#
# The manifest sha256 quoted in STATUS.md and in the reports, and the per-file
# code_sha256_prefix that to_run.py writes into the provenance record of every
# run, are hashes of the working-tree bytes. Without this file a Windows clone
# checks out CRLF and every one of those hashes changes, so two collaborators
# running identical code would record different provenance. Pinning eol=lf keeps
# the quoted hashes reproducible everywhere.
#
# text=auto still detects binary content and leaves it untouched; the .gz
# artefact is marked binary explicitly as well.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.gz binary
